    "result_text": "The build is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI changed the `customerCode` format from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` and rebuilt everything derived from it.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:**\n- `generateCustomerCode` now takes both `city` and `lastName`. It builds `CITY3` (upper-cased first three letters of the city) and `LAST3` (first three of the last name), then appends a **per-city** 4-digit sequence \u2014 one more than the number of owners already registered in that city (`countOwnersInCity`), instead of the old global owner count.\n- Added a shared `firstThreeLetters` helper (letters-only, upper-cased) used for both segments, and `countOwnersInCity`, which counts existing owners with a matching city using the same case-insensitive/whitespace-collapsed normalization (`normalizeHouseholdField`) already used elsewhere in the controller.\n- The **membership number** rebuilds automatically: `generateMembershipNumber` is fed the new `customerCode`, so it becomes `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>-M<YY>` (e.g. `SYD-SMI-0007-M26`) without further change.\n\n**`openapi.yml`:** Updated the `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` descriptions and examples to reflect the new format.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreCustomerCodeHasCityPrefix` (asserting the `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}` shape) passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures/errors).",
